export anchor TriageFirstStyle:
    number: 197
    screen: ProjectsDashboard
    name: Triage first
    idea: The home screen is an inbox for problems, where a red headed Needs attention list leads with overdue, behind and at risk work and offers the next action on each row, while the healthy projects follow as a quiet table and the week's numbers sit in a right rail.
    base: light
    palette:
        page: #f6f7f8, the page behind the boxes
        card: #ffffff, boxes, the tab bar and fields
        ink: #1c2026, text
        muted: #5a616b, hints, meta and axis text
        line: #d9dce1, borders, never text
        graphite: #24292f, the header, action buttons and this week bars
        headText: #e6e9ed, text on the graphite header
        lastWeek: #7d848f, last week bars
        focus: #0b5cd5, the focus ring only
        green: #1a7f45, On track with a check disc
        amber: #8a4b00, At risk with a triangle on #fff5e0
        red: #b42318, Behind with a chevron square and overdue with a clock on #fdf0ef
    type:
        One stack, Segoe UI, system-ui, Roboto, Noto Sans, Helvetica Neue,
        Arial. The greeting is 20px bold, KPI figures 18px bold tabular,
        triage titles 15px bold, body 14px at 1.45, facts and feed 13px, and
        buttons and tags 12 to 13px at 600 to 700.
    layout:
        A graphite header bar holds a white hexagon mark with the brand, a
        dark search field, a white New project button, an outlined bell
        with a red count and initials with Mara Okafor. A white tab bar
        beneath it carries the six nav links with a graphite underline on
        Home. A one line greeting with the date says the 4 overdue tasks
        lead the list. The body splits into a wide left column and a 340px
        right rail. On the left, the Needs attention box has a red tinted
        head with a triangle and a count of 3. Its rows each carry a 4px
        red or amber left edge, a 24px solid severity glyph, a title with
        an outlined status tag, one line of detail with a mini bar, a line
        of facts such as days left, tasks to go and target pace, and two
        buttons at the right, a graphite primary and an outlined secondary
        such as Review tasks and Reassign, Open and Change date, or Open and
        Message team. Under it an On track box with a green check and a
        count of 4 is a quiet table of the healthy projects with progress,
        due with days left, status and an Open button. The right rail
        stacks a This week list of the four numbers with overdue first in
        red, a compact 14 day bar chart with grey last week and graphite
        this week, and the activity feed. Below 1060px the rail drops under
        the main column in two columns, and on phones everything stacks and
        buttons wrap under each triage row.
    spacing: 4px and 8px steps. 12 to 16px row padding and 20px between boxes.
    density: High. Compact 34px controls and 14px text, built for working through a list.
    corners: 6px on boxes, buttons and fields, and 4px on tags.
    borders: 1px grey boxes, with a 4px left edge in the severity colour on every triage row.
    shadows: None.
    icons:
        Solid 24px severity glyphs lead each triage row, a clock disc for
        overdue, a chevron square for Behind and a triangle for At risk.
        Status tags are outlined and hold a solid check disc, triangle or
        chevron square plus the word. Line icons at 1.8px elsewhere.
    focus: A solid 2px blue outline offset 2px, light blue on the dark header.
    tone: Direct and action led, such as Review tasks, Change date and No action needed.
